ho it is that I'm going to vote  for here in Massachusetts but I will  tell you rest assured another post from  the David Pakman show subreddit Dave  Rubin I am now pro-life yes there  a cultural critic and arbiter of ideas  named Dave Rubin who interviews people  from all over the political spectrum  mostly right-wingers and he has talked  about how he didn't leave the left the  left left him but his views have  actually been changing and the latest in  this evolution is that he now says that  he is no longer an atheist and I saw a  video where he said he's still mostly  secular but believes there's something  bigger and it seemed like a way to  basically ride the fence so that you  don't have to in a completely  embarrassing way say my view has changed  180 degrees which for a 40 year old to  have that kind of Awakening is is odd is  to say the least but he claims he's had  it fine he's found a way to ride the  fence which is to say he's still mostly  secular but he now believes that there  is something bigger and that it seems  like it'll kind of placate the the right  wing of religious folks that  increasingly follow him and so the  prediction here from this user on our  subreddit is Dave Rubin will eventually  come out as pro-life and being against  abortion wouldn't be surprised if it'd  be funnier if he came out and said he  was no longer gay that that actually  would be more of an awakening but I  don't expect that to happen and I would  not be shocked if he comes out and says  he is now pro-life also from the David  Pakman show subreddit Pete Buddha jej  releases a list of McKinsey clients and  that list includes blook Blue Cross Blue  Shield of Michigan and the Department of  Defense so listen I've already said that  Pete Budaj is not a progressive he's  really a Biden centrist that's what he  is he's not been hiding it his views on  campaign finance reform are not  particularly progressive we had video of  that for you earlier this week I think  that it's